From 866d931af78d6fffb8e51704d051b8bc9c421db5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:04:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vm): hibernate persistent VMs after N idle minutes and
 restart on next exec

Persistent per-user VMs kept running (and holding host CPU/memory) even
when nobody used them. VmManager now tracks the last activity per user and
an idle sweeper stops VMs that have been idle for longer than
SWARM_VM_IDLE_MIN (default 30, 0 disables).

- lib/vm/idle.ts: idle policy (SWARM_VM_IDLE_MIN, SWARM_VM_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SEC)
- lib/vm/manager.ts: activity tracking (touch/lastActivityAt/idleForMs/
  isIdle/hasActiveExec), sweepIdle() that hibernates idle VMs under the
  per-user write lock, and re-ensure on the next exec so the container is
  restarted with its /workspace volume intact
- lib/vm/idle-sweeper.ts: timer-driven sweeper with injectable clock and
  interval functions; wired into the runtime singleton
- A VM with a running exec is never stopped: the sweep skips users with an
  exec in flight and re-checks the activity record under the write lock
- Tests (FakeVmDriver + fake timers) prove stop+wake with the volume
  preserved, that a running exec is never stopped, and that an exec racing
  a sweep keeps its VM alive
